; ============================================================
; TITLE:    House from Square and Triangle
; CATEGORY: Classic Logo
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     procedures, debugging, Mindstorms, filling
; SUMMARY:  The famous first project: put SQUARE and TRIANGLE together to make a house, find the bug, and fix it.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   On the left you see a first try at a house: the roof has ended up
;   inside the walls. On the right is the fixed house, colored in, with
;   a door, a window and a chimney.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Then type  clean square 100  or  clean triangle 100  or
;   clean house 100  in the command center and watch each piece.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * teaching the turtle new words with TO ... END
;   * using your own words to build bigger ones
;   * a "bug" is just a surprise you can understand and fix
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make a street of houses of different sizes with REPEAT.
;   * Add a second window next to the first.
;   * Change the roof so it is a taller, pointier triangle.
; ============================================================

; In Mindstorms (1980) Seymour Papert tells this story. A child who
; knows SQUARE and TRIANGLE types SQUARE TRIANGLE to get a house, and
; the triangle comes out inside the square. Nothing is "wrong" with the
; computer: the turtle did exactly what it was told. Thinking about where
; the turtle is, and which way it faces, finds the fix. Papert used this
; to show that bugs are something to learn from, not to be ashamed of.

to square :size
  repeat 4 [forward :size right 90]
end

to triangle :size
  repeat 3 [forward :size right 120]
end

; The first try. SQUARE leaves the turtle at the bottom left corner
; facing up, so TRIANGLE starts there too and turns into the square.
to buggy.house :size
  square :size
  triangle :size
end

; The fix: walk up to the top of the wall, turn 30 degrees so the
; triangle points up instead of in, draw it, then go back home.
to house :size
  square :size
  forward :size
  right 30
  triangle :size
  left 30
  back :size
end

; The colored house. Each FILLED shape covers what is already on the
; screen, so we work like a painter: the big wall first, then the door
; and window on top of it. The chimney goes up before the roof, so the
; roof hides the bottom of the chimney.
to fancy.house :size
  localmake "x xcor
  localmake "y ycor
  setpencolor 0
  ; walls
  filled [250 220 150] [square :size]
  ; door
  penup setxy :x + :size * 0.15 :y setheading 0 pendown
  filled [140 80 40] [square2 :size * 0.22 :size * 0.45]
  ; window
  penup setxy :x + :size * 0.55 :y + :size * 0.5 setheading 0 pendown
  filled [180 220 255] [square :size * 0.25]
  ; chimney, standing on top of the wall
  penup setxy :x + :size * 0.7 :y + :size setheading 0 pendown
  filled [120 120 130] [square2 :size * 0.12 :size * 0.8]
  ; roof, the same way as in HOUSE
  penup setxy :x :y setheading 0 pendown
  forward :size right 30
  filled [200 60 50] [triangle :size]
end

; a rectangle, used for the door and the chimney
to square2 :width :height
  repeat 2 [forward :height right 90 forward :width right 90]
end

to caption :x :text
  penup setxy :x -200 setheading 0
  setpencolor 0
  label :text
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [235 245 255]
setpensize 3
setlabelheight 18
penup setxy -320 -120 pendown
setpencolor [200 50 50]
buggy.house 160
caption -330 [square triangle: oops!]
penup setxy 100 -120 pendown
fancy.house 200
caption 110 [the fixed house]
